s out to her  friends and family and Tyler finds  himself wondering why he can't seem to  land a date the series stars several  fresh faces including Jahi Winston as  Luke and Quinn Liebling as Tyler  alongside more familiar names like  Sydney Sweeney as Emily with a realistic  storyline a heaping of nineties cultural  references and a charming cast  everything sucked makes for something of  a single season gem set on a remote  Welsh Island in 1905 the terrifying  period drama apostle follows Thomas  Richardson as he attempts to rescue his  sister Jennifer from a secretive  religious cults in order to prize some  secrets out of cult members who might be  willing to reveal more than they should  Thomas disguises himself as a curious  convert and eventually finds out that  Jennifer is being held for ransom from  there a gruesome battle for the future  of the island ensues and if you get a  bit squeamish at the sight of blood well  you may want to keep your eyes shut but  while apostle might be gory it's not for  mere shock value this film is a bonafide  psychological thriller all the way  through this please this community it's  broken that was such the fascinating  mythology built around the cult explores  the dark side of the Divine Feminine and  the open-ended conclusion will it once  satisfy viewers and leave them pondering  kiss me first is an experimental series  which alternates between the real and  the surreal as it flips from live-action  to virtual reality Laila is a lonely  teenager who spends most of her days  playing the MMORPG azana  in which she meets a more confident girl  named test who pulls her out of her  shell the two eventually become close  offline but when test disappears laila  takes it upon herself to solve the  mystery and quickly learns that virtual  actions can have real-world consequences  the series is based on the Lottie Moga  novel of the same title and with skin's  creator Brian else Lee at the helm you  just know you're in for plenty of juicy  drama no supposed to be cruel I'm not  I'm a friend and I'm here  kiss me first has echoes of Black Mirror  another sci-fi series which explored the  pitfalls of human reliance on technology  and its uncanny valley style of CGI  makes it hard not to question your own  relationship to your screens you might  want to spend a little time outside  after this one based on the novel of  Cornelia by Florencia at Chevy's hair  DITA is a solid thriller that begins by  inviting the viewer into a setting that  establishes a genuine sense of impending  doom and then establishes a tone which  never quite lets up throughout the rest  of the film pipa a policewoman whose  friend pinellia went missing in  Patagonia as a teenager feels like she  can't find peace until she solves the  mystery behind her disappearance but  she sets out to discover what really  happened to her friend on that fateful  day she realizes that the search might  be putting her own life in danger  although the plot can drag a bit during  the scenes in which people in gross tin  paperwork he'll still remain gripped  until the very last moment  [Music]
 

